================================================================================
DUAL LICENSE STRUCTURE
================================================================================

This project is released under a dual licensing model. You may choose either
license according to your use case:

  1) Open Source License — GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0)
     File: LICENSE.AGPL-3.0
     SPDX: AGPL-3.0-only / AGPL-3.0-or-later

  2) Commercial License — Proprietary, for closed-source / SaaS / enterprise
     File: COMMERCIAL_NOTICE.md (summary) + separate commercial agreement
     SPDX: LicenseRef-PolyRust-Commercial

You must comply with the terms of the license you choose. You may not combine
permissions from both licenses.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Option 1: AGPL-3.0 (Open Source)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Use this if you are building open source software, research, education, or
personal projects and you are willing to comply with AGPL-3.0 obligations.

Key obligations under AGPL-3.0 (see LICENSE.AGPL-3.0 for full text):

  - If you modify PolyRust and allow users to interact with it over a network
    (e.g., SaaS, web service, API), you MUST make the complete Corresponding
    Source of your modified version available to those users, including all
    changes, via a network server at no charge (Section 13).
  - You must preserve copyright notices and license notices.
  - You must license the entire derived work under AGPL-3.0.
  - No warranty, no liability (Sections 15-16).

This is the same license used by many copyleft network projects. It ensures
that improvements remain open.

Core promise still holds: `core/` crate has zero third-party dependencies
(std-only). All third-party dependencies are isolated in `frontends/*`.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Option 2: Commercial License (Proprietary)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Use this if you cannot comply with AGPL-3.0, for example:

  - You want to embed PolyRust in a closed-source product
  - You run PolyRust as a service without releasing source
  - You need warranty, indemnity, or enterprise support
  - You need to avoid AGPL-3.0 network copyleft

Commercial license grants you:

  - Right to use, modify, and distribute without AGPL-3.0 source disclosure
  - Right to run as SaaS / on-prem without network source offer
  - Optional SLA, support, and custom features
  - Patent grant (negotiable)

See COMMERCIAL_NOTICE.md for summary of rights and responsibilities, and how
to obtain a commercial license.

Contact: TBA (commercial-licensing channel announced before first commercial
release) — meanwhile open an issue titled "[Commercial License Request]" in
the repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why Dual License?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - AGPL-3.0 guarantees that the community benefits from improvements, especially
    for network server use (the core of PolyRust's QAP / Groebner / CDCL pipeline).
  - Commercial license allows sustainable funding for Lean formal proofs,
    F4/F5 optimization, and audit report generation, while letting enterprises
    use PolyRust in proprietary contexts.

  This model is used by MongoDB (SSPL/Commercial), Elastic (Elastic/Commercial),
  and many formal verification tools.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-Party Dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - `core/` — zero third-party, std-only, fully covered by this dual license.
  - `frontends/*` — may depend on third-party crates (axum, tokio, syn, ureq,
    etc.) under their own licenses (MIT/Apache-2.0). Those dependencies are NOT
    covered by PolyRust's commercial license; you must comply with their licenses.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
How to Apply
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  At the top of each source file, include:

    // PolyRust — Dual Licensed: AGPL-3.0 OR Commercial
    // Copyright (C) 2024-2026 PolyRust Team
    // See LICENSE and COMMERCIAL_NOTICE.md

  Or for Lean:

    /- PolyRust — Dual Licensed: AGPL-3.0 OR Commercial -/

  The full AGPL-3.0 text is in LICENSE.AGPL-3.0.

